@moonsand/dsh-desktop-restart README · Requirements：- **Windows only.** The restart path is built on the Windows Task Scheduler and Windows Script Host.
- DeepSeek Harness desktop `0.2.1-rc.2` or newer (declared in `engines.dsh`; tested on `0.2.2-rc.1`), Node `>=20`.
- No npm dependencies. `index.js` imports only Node built-ins; `client.js` imports `react`, provided by the shell.

@moonsand/dsh-desktop-restart README · Plugin market index (self-hosted)：1. Push the repository to GitHub; the index URL is `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MoonSand/dsh-desktop-restart/main/market/index.json` (GitHub Pages works too).
2. Plugins → **Discover** → **Add index source**, then paste that https URL. Index sources accept `http:` / `https:` only, without credentials or a fragment.
3. Cards show the bilingual title and description — the index stores `description` as an `{ "en": …, "zh": … }` object and **must contain `en`**; a Chinese-only value is rejected by the validator. Installing uses the exact npm version.

@moonsand/dsh-desktop-restart README · How the restart works：1. A **detached** `powershell.exe` starts but never runs its `-EncodedCommand` script — silently, with no error. The helper is spawned as a plain child instead.
2. Every process the Host starts inherits Chromium's **job object** with kill-on-close, so anything the Host spawns dies with the application's main process. A helper that kills first and launches afterwards dies between those two steps.
3. The **Task Scheduler** service resolves launches in its own process, outside that job, which is the only way to leave something running that outlives the kill.
